    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **Tests run: 54, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** and **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system, keeping the OfficeFloor derivation pattern (a `common` helper invoked at mapping time).\n\n**`Membership.java`** \u2014 now computes points from 0:\n- +2 email present, +1 `namesakeCount == 0`, +2 household of 3+ (`householdMemberCount >= 3`), +3 tenure over 365 days.\n- `pointsOf(owner)` returns the raw points; `levelOf(owner)` maps them: 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipPoints` mapping (`Membership.pointsOf(owner)`) alongside the existing `membershipLevel` mapping so both fields are returned.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema field (generates the DTO getter/setter) and updated `membershipLevel` (max raised 3\u21924, description rewritten to describe the points mapping).\n\nThe new household +2 award is what lets a 3-member household reach 5 points \u2192 level 3 (Cp23/Cp39), while a fresh emailed owner scores 3 \u2192 level 2 (Cp15/Cp24/Cp40). A new owner's zero tenure keeps the +3 out of reach, so level 4 remains unreachable at creation.",
