    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, taken from `owners.POST.yml` and each function class. Every step runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all reads/writes share one transaction that commits once at the very end.\n\n## 0. Authorization (before any step)\n- `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` \u2014 caller lacking the role is rejected (403 via `AuthorizationDeniedException` handler).\n\n## 1. `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2014 validation + in-place normalization\nRuns several things in this internal order:\n1. **Normalize address** \u2014 trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations; written back onto the request.\n2. **Blank checks** \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city` rejected if null/blank (address checked *after* normalization, so whitespace-only fails here).\n3. **Normalize telephone \u2192 E.164** \u2014 strip separators; keep `+`+country code, else assume `+61` and drop a leading `0`; enforce 8\u201315 digits and country-specific national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Failure adds a `telephone` error; success is written back.\n4. **Schema constraints** \u2014 `validator.validate(request)` (`@Email`, `@Pattern`, `@Size`/max-length, etc.); each violating field added to errors.\n5. **Postcode range check** (only if present and well-formed) \u2014 must be in range for the region derived from `city` (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city accepts any 4-digit).\n6. If any errors accumulated \u2192 throw `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (**400**).\n7. **Normalize email** \u2014 if present, lower-cased and written back.\n8. Publishes the (now normalized) `OwnerFieldsDto` for later steps.\n\n## 2. `RejectDisposableEmailDomain` \u2014 validation\n- If email present, extract domain; if it's on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (**400**).\n\n## 3. `RejectFutureRegistrationDate` \u2014 validation\n- If supplied `registrationDate` is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**). Absent date is allowed.\n\n## 4. `ResolveRegistrationDate` \u2014 side-effect (derives state)\n- Effective date = supplied date or today; **rolled forward** past Sat/Sun to Monday. Published as a `LocalDate` variable used by the daily-limit, build, and bulk-signup steps.\n\n## 5. `RejectDuplicateIdentity` \u2014 validation (reads all owners)\n- Computes `householdId` (from last name + postcode) and full `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`).\n- **Identity duplicate** \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**), always.\n- **Household duplicate** (same householdId as an existing owner) \u2192 **409**, *unless* `sharesHousehold: true`.\n\n## 6. `RejectCityAtCapacity` \u2014 validation (reads all owners)\n- If the city (case-insensitive) already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n## 7. `RejectDailyOwnerLimit` \u2014 validation (reads all owners)\n- If \u2265 100 owners already carry the resolved business-day `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**).\n\n## 8. `BuildOwner` \u2014 side-effect\n- Maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity; overwrites its registration date with the resolved business-day value.\n\n## 9. `AssignCustomerCode` \u2014 side-effect (mutates entity)\n- Sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; hash8 = first 8 upper hex of `SHA-256(telephone+lastName)`).\n\n## 10. `AssignMembershipNumber` \u2014 side-effect\n- Sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (YY = last two digits of registration-date year).\n\n## 11. `AssignHousehold` \u2014 side-effect\n- Sets `householdId` deterministically from last name + postcode (unconditional, even for lone owners).\n\n## 12. `AssignHouseholdSize` \u2014 side-effect (reads all owners)\n- Sets `householdMemberCount` = existing members sharing the householdId + 1 (this owner). Null householdId \u2192 1.\n\n## 13. `AssignNamesakeCount` \u2014 side-effect (reads all owners)\n- Sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive); the new owner excluded (not yet persisted).\n\n## 14. `AssignBulkSignupWarning` \u2014 side-effect (reads all owners)\n- Sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if > 80 owners already share the business-day registration date.\n\n## 15. `AssignPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 side-effect (reads all owners)\n- If `sharesHousehold: true` \u2192 sets `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`.\n- Else finds existing owner with same lastName (case-insensitive) + postcode but *different* telephone; sets `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf` to the lowest matching id (or false/null if none).\n\n## 16. `SaveOwner` \u2014 side-effect (persistence)\n- `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 persists, generating the id.\n\n## 17. `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 side-effect (logging)\n- Logs to the `AUDIT` logger: owner id, customerCode, registrationDate, and computed membership level.\n\n## 18. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` \u2014 side-effect (response)\n- Maps to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Transaction commit** happens once here at the end of the pipeline.\n\n---\n\nA couple of things worth flagging: several rejection checks (duplicate, city capacity, daily limit) and the count/flag assignments each call `ownerRepository.findAll()` independently \u2014 the validations run in the fixed order above (identity \u2192 city \u2192 daily limit), so the error a bad request gets depends on that ordering. Also note `sharesHousehold` only bypasses the *household*-duplicate branch in step 5, never a full identity duplicate."
